1. e4 e5 2. f4 exf4 3. Nf3 Be7 4. Bc4 Bh4+ 5. Kf1 d5 {Both sides have what they wanted from the opening. The middlegame will be about the centre.} 6. exd5 Bg4 7. Nc3 Ne7 8. d3 ! Ng6 {The critical moment. The pieces are as good as they are going to get; something has to happen now.} (8... Bxf3 Rb1 Bxd1 {was the alternative — playable, but it hands over the initiative.}) 9. g3 O-O 10. Kg2 Nd7 11. Ne4 Nde5 ?! 12. Ned2 Qf6 13. Rf1 Rae8 14. Bb3 h5 15. Ne4 Qf5 16. Nd4 Qd7 17. Qe1 Bh3+ 18. Kh1 Bxf1 19. Qxf1 fxg3 20. hxg3 Bd8 21. Nf5 h4 22. Qh3 c6 23. dxc6 Qxc6 24. Bf4 Nxf4 25. gxf4 Ng6 26. Qg4 Rxe4 27. dxe4 Qxe4+ 28. Kh2 Re8 29. Rg1 Qe2+ 30. Rg2 Qe4 31. Qxg6 Qxf4+ 32. Kh3 Qf3+ 33. Kh2 Qf4+ 34. Kh1 Bf6 35. Qxf7+ Kh8 36. Qh5+ Qh6 37. Nxh6 gxh6 {The endgame is winning but not simple — the passed pawn needs its king, not just its rook.} 38. Qxe8+ 1-0
